# VED ownership

Canon: `docs/knowledge/branches.md` · `src/lib/ved/PACKAGES.md` · `plan-parallel-ownership.md` · ADR **D36**.

| Area | Put code in |
|------|-------------|
| Client / broker / manufacturer panes | `src/components/ved/{client,broker,manufacturer}/*` |
| Cabinets | orchestration only (`*Cabinet.tsx`) |
| Session API | `app/api/v1/*` · domain extract `containers/api` |
| domain / orch / mesh / draft | see `PACKAGES.md` |
| `containers/llm` · `containers/ocr` | **LBM-owned** Compose services (D36 — no nested `./llm` sync) |

## D36 — zero coupling to taurus / nested `./llm` (always)

Changes to **this** project (ibm-cargo / LBM) or **its** database must **not** affect:

- files under **taurus/llm**, sibling `../llm`, **nested `./llm`**, or external matrix clone;
- databases, Docker volumes, or secrets belonging to that matrix project.

Allowed: call matrix over HTTP (`*_SERVICE_URL`) only.  
Forbidden: `sync:ai-matrix` copy; mount/build defaults on `./llm`; edit matrix sources; `prisma` against matrix DB; shared `DATABASE_URL`.

## Multi-model

- **Model ≠ container.** Vendors = `AI_CHAIN_ID` / env profiles in LBM (`src/lib/ved/chains/`).
- **Capability = service** (classification, ocr, …). One HTTP envelope each.
- UI never calls matrix URLs.

## Forbidden

- `@prisma/client` in `containers/{broker,client,admin,manufacturer}`
- Parallel C3+C4 extracts in one change (D19)
- Docker service per vendor
- Touching taurus/llm or nested `./llm` from an LBM/DB changeset (D36)
- Reintroducing sync from nested `./llm` into `containers/{llm,ocr}`
